<title>RUSSIA: Russian 168-day T-bill yields 34.81 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 168-day T-bill yields 34.81 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an additional tranche of 168-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 34.81 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The original issue of the bills closed at 86.07 on Tuesday, to yield 34.95 percent.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in a 33.44-35.85 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		   22071 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    4.00 trln</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  6.22 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		  3.54 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  3.05 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		   86.19 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 86.07 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		   34.81 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	35.16 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	     168 days</p>
<p>    Original issue date	   February 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   August 27, 1997</p>
<p>On March 5 the Finance Ministry raised 4.30 trillion roubles by selling 357-day T-bill, making total proceeds from today's auctions 7.35 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It had also repaid about 375.58 billion roubles in interest on OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24007) and paid 6.92 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22056).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
